The circumference of a sphere is the same as the circumference of a great circle of the sphere, which is given by $2\pi r$. Given that the circumference is $12\pi$, we can find the radius $r$ of the sphere: \[
2\pi r = 12\pi \implies r = \frac{12\pi}{2\pi} = 6 \text{ inches}
\]

The volume of the entire sphere is given by \[
V = \frac{4}{3}\pi r^3 = \frac{4}{3}\pi (6^3) = \frac{4}{3}\pi \cdot 216 = 288\pi \text{ cubic inches}
\]

The volume of one wedge is one-fourth of the volume of the sphere since the sphere is divided into four congruent wedges: \[
V_{\text{wedge}} = \frac{1}{4} \cdot 288\pi = 72\pi \text{ cubic inches}
\]

So, the volume of one wedge is \(\boxed{72\pi}\) cubic inches. </think> <answer>72\pi </answer>

